  "title": "Clubhouse Cruiser",
  "date": "2025-06-03",
  "excerpt": "Blending road-trip versatility with daily comfort, the Clubhouse Cruiser was designed on a Mercedes Sprinter 170 chassis to handle everything from long-term travel to weekend getaways. Built with an 800Ah lithium battery",
  "body": [
    "Blending road-trip versatility with daily comfort, the Clubhouse Cruiser was designed on a Mercedes Sprinter 170 chassis to handle everything from long-term travel to weekend getaways. Built with an 800Ah lithium battery bank, 300W solar system, 3000W pure sine inverter, and DC-DC charging, this van powers modern essentials with ease. Whether you’re working remotely from the PopRak rooftop tent or just recharging at basecamp, the electrical system is built to support life on the move—complete with microwave, fridge, and multiple USB/AC outlets throughout the cabin.",
    "The design prioritizes usability and relaxation. Inside, you’ll find a wet-bath style indoor shower with a dry flush toilet, a rear outdoor shower, and a kitchen fitted with a stainless undermount sink, Isotherm Cruise 130 refrigerator with freezer, and acacia butcher block countertop. While this particular van skips the induction cooktop, the layout remains fully functional for travelers who prefer external or portable cooking. Paired with natural wood finishes, painted shiplap siding, and soft LED lighting, the space balances warmth with utility.",
    "What sets the Clubhouse Cruiser apart is its combination of lifestyle flexibility and rugged upgrades. A PopRak rooftop tent with interior pass-through provides additional sleeping space and ventilation, while the Agile Off Road lift kit, Owl spare tire carrier, and full all-terrain tire package make it trail-ready. Add in the exterior perimeter lighting, 50” LED light bar, and basic side steps, and this rig is set up for late-night arrivals and early-morning departures—wherever the road leads.",
    "Inside, two additional captain’s chairs create a true lounge-style layout, perfect for family road trips or multi-passenger outings. A queen memory foam bed, swivel seating, headliner shelf, and dual pullout gear trays make every corner of the van feel intuitive. Whether you’re chasing mountain air or camping under city lights, the Clubhouse Cruiser offers the best of both worlds—off-grid functionality with all-day livability."
  ],
